{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And of Dan he said: Dan is a lion's whelp.</b> Since Jacob said, ״דָּן יָדִין עַמּוֹ״, and every judge needs to be mighty as a lion, as it says (Exodus 18:21): ״וְאַתָּה תֶחֱזֶה מִכָּל הָעָם אַנְשֵׁי חַיִל״, so that he not tremble before litigants if there is among them some powerful figure. Therefore he said of Dan that he would be ״גּוּר אַרְיֵה יְזַנֵּק מִן הַבָּשָׁן״ — the Bashan is a place of evil beasts of prey; so too the judge — his entire engagement is to snatch prey from among the bulls of Bashan, to rescue the prey from their hand. Therefore the judge must himself have a heart like the heart of a lion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The phrase כָּךְ הַדַּיָּן כָּל קִלּוּסוֹ is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. The word קִלּוּסוֹ (his praise/laudation) does not fit the context smoothly and may be corrupt; the sense appears to be 'all his engagement/concern.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:40.843414502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}